{
  "id": "newman-verses-on-various-occasions",
  "cover": "classic",
  "name": {
    "en-US": "Verses on Various Occasions",
    "pt-BR": "Versos em Várias Ocasiões"
  },
  "author": {
    "en-US": "John Henry Newman",
    "pt-BR": "John Henry Newman"
  },
  "description": {
    "en-US": "Newman's collected poems, 1818 to 1865, as he gathered them in 1867 and dedicated to his friend Badeley: the verses of his Oxford youth, the poems of the Mediterranean voyage of 1832-33 including Lead, Kindly Light, the Lyra Apostolica pieces of the Oxford Movement, and the hymns and poems of his Catholic years. The Dream of Gerontius, which belongs to the same volume, is a book of its own.",
    "pt-BR": "Os poemas reunidos de Newman, de 1818 a 1865, como ele os recolheu em 1867 e dedicou ao amigo Badeley: os versos de sua juventude em Oxford, os poemas da viagem ao Mediterrâneo de 1832-33, entre eles Lead, Kindly Light, as peças da Lyra Apostolica do Movimento de Oxford e os hinos e poemas de seus anos católicos. O Sonho de Gerôncio, que pertence ao mesmo volume, é um livro à parte."
  },
  "composed": "1818-1865",
  "languages": [
    "en-US"
  ],
  "work": "newman/verses-on-various-occasions",
  "editions": {
    "en-US": {
      "editor": "John Henry Newman (Longmans, new impression of 1903; Newman Reader)",
      "year": 1867
    }
  },
  "sources": [
    {
      "language": "en-US",
      "url": "https://www.newmanreader.org/works/verses/index.html",
      "edition": "Verses on Various Occasions (London: Burns, Oates, 1868; Longmans, Green new impression 1903), as transcribed by the Newman Reader.",
      "description": "178 chapters: Newman Reader page numbers, navigation and its editorial remarks are dropped; Newman's own notes are kept as footnotes. One chapter per poem, numbered as in the volume; line breaks kept as hard breaks, with long lines the page had wrapped rejoined. The Dream of Gerontius (its own book) and the Dublin Review notice are left out. The Latin appendices (hymns and the prologues to Terence) are left out. Raw page text in sources/en-US-originals/.",
      "tier": "A",
      "tierEvidence": "Public domain: Newman died in 1890 and the text is of a Longmans impression (or earlier edition) before 1930. The Newman Reader page footers claim copyright in the site's transcription (c) 2007 NINS; a plain transcription of a public-domain text adds no authorship under US law."
    }
  ],
